<div class="card">
  <h2>Weekend pay</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Saturday and Sunday loads are settled at <b>driver 70% / company 30%</b> of net (separate from the weekday 50/50).</li>
    <li>Condition: you must work both that week and the following week — two weeks total — with no absence. If the condition is not met, those loads are settled at 50/50.</li>
    <li>Saturday/Sunday loads pay the driver 70% of net when the driver works both weeks with no absence.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Pay split by tenure</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>First 3 months after hire: <b>driver 45% / company 55%</b></li>
    <li>After 3 months: <b>driver 50% / company 50%</b></li>
    <li>After 1 year: <b>driver 55% / company 45%</b></li>
    <li>The weekend 70% rule applies separately from the tenure steps.</li>
    <li>Your split steps up automatically at 3 months and at 1 year.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Overweight restriction (net weight)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>20 ft container: up to <b>39,000 lbs</b></li>
    <li>40 ft container: up to <b>45,000 lbs</b></li>
    <li>Reefer 40 ft: up to <b>44,000 lbs</b></li>
    <li>Over the limit, the load is treated as Overweight and the lane O/W rate (table above) applies.</li>
  </ul>
</div>
